{"name":"Bewitching Blue","hex":"#bbd0e3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bewitching","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act by which somebody is bewitched; a curse or enchantment."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Enchanting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bewitching"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Incantation","blocks":[{"text":"An incantation, spell, charm, enchantment, or bewitchery is a magical formula intended to trigger a magical effect on a person or objects. The formula can be spoken, sung, or chanted. An incantation can also be performed during ceremonial rituals or prayers. In the world of magic, wizards, witches, and fairies are common performers of incantations in culture and folklore."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Book_of_incantations_f.7v.png/330px-Book_of_incantations_f.7v.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incantation"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg/500px-The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg/500px-The_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_%281889%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Enchanted Garden of Messer Ansaldo by Marie Spartali Stillman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Enchanted_Garden_of_Messer_Ansaldo_by_Marie_Spartali_Stillman_(1889).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg/250px-Abracadabra_triangle_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Classic magic words","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbracadabra_triangle_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Orlando_F